ds, O LORD; consider my groaning.","verse":1}],"id":"David","label":"David","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"David::David::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"David","term":"David"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"David","sourceTitle":"David"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"For the choirmaster, to be accompanied by flutes. A Psalm of David. Give ear to my words, O LORD; consider my groaning.","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"In the morning, O LORD, You hear my voice; at daybreak I lay my plea before You and wait in expectation.","verse":3},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"You destroy those who tell lies; the LORD abhors the man of bloodshed and deceit.","verse":6},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Lead me, O LORD, in Your righteousness because of my enemies; make straight Your way before me.","verse":8},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"For surely You, O LORD, bless the righteous; You surround them with the shield of Your favor.","verse":12}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.1-7.17","r":"Ps.3.1-7.17","rawR":"Ps.3.1-7.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.1-7.17","value":"Ps.3.1-7.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 3–7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This group of psalms moves readers from the orderly world of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.1.1-2.12","r":"Ps.1.1-2.12","rawR":"Ps.1.1-2.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.1.1-2.12","value":"Ps.1.1-2.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 1–2"}," to a disoriented one. The Lord’s anointed cries out while facing enemies, ferocious opposition, evil schemes, and the Lord’s apparent distance."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.3.1-7.17","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":7,"endVerse":17,"startChapter":3,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.3.1-7.17","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[3,4,5,6,7],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"979e35739df35cd8a906cb35ce271f91dc796183d42ddf70cbc0fa127889810f","sourceItemName":"Ps.3.1-7.17","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5981,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.3.1-7.17","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.3.1-7.17","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.1-12","r":"Ps.5.1-12","rawR":"Ps.5.1-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.1-12","value":"Ps.5.1-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This morning prayer (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.3","r":"Ps.5.3","rawR":"Ps.5.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.3","value":"Ps.5.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:3"},") expresses unwavering confidence in the Lord’s help and protection. The psalmist asks for and awaits God’s response (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.1-3","r":"Ps.5.1-3","rawR":"Ps.5.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.1-3","value":"Ps.5.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:1-3"},"). He describes the schemes of the wicked in detail but does not get lost in his circumstances. The psalmist also knows that the wicked cannot coexist with God (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.4-6","r":"Ps.5.4-6","rawR":"Ps.5.4-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.4-6","value":"Ps.5.4-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:4-6"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.9","r":"Ps.5.9","rawR":"Ps.5.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.9","value":"Ps.5.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"9"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.1.5","r":"Ps.1.5","rawR":"Ps.1.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.1.5","value":"Ps.1.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:5"},"). He keeps returning to the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.7-8","r":"Ps.5.7-8","rawR":"Ps.5.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.7-8","value":"Ps.5.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:7-8"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.10","r":"Ps.5.10","rawR":"Ps.5.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.10","value":"Ps.5.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"10"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.1-3","r":"Ps.5.1-3","rawR":"Ps.5.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.1-3","value":"Ps.5.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:1-3"},"), and then he prays for the godly community (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.10-12","r":"Ps.5.10-12","rawR":"Ps.5.10-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.10-12","value":"Ps.5.10-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:10-12"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.8","r":"Ps.3.8","rawR":"Ps.3.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.8","value":"Ps.3.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.1-12","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":12,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.1-12","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"211b550322fc18ebe7acd82c7a2543530e882b62d81db75bc04926c799015f8e","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.1-12","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5997,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.1-12","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.1-12","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.1-2","r":"Ps.5.1-2","rawR":"Ps.5.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.1-2","value":"Ps.5.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:1-2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The request ",{"c":["hear me"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," appears in several prayers as a call for God’s attention during a time of trouble (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.39.12","r":"Ps.39.12","rawR":"Ps.39.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.39.12","value":"Ps.39.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"39:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.84.8","r":"Ps.84.8","rawR":"Ps.84.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.84.8","value":"Ps.84.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"84:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.143.1","r":"Ps.143.1","rawR":"Ps.143.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.143.1","value":"Ps.143.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"143:1"},"), as does ",{"c":["pay attention"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.17.1","r":"Ps.17.1","rawR":"Ps.17.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.17.1","value":"Ps.17.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.54.2","r":"Ps.54.2","rawR":"Ps.54.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.54.2","value":"Ps.54.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"54:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.130.2","r":"Ps.130.2","rawR":"Ps.130.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.130.2","value":"Ps.130.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"130:2"},"). The needy ask their God, “Are you listening?”"],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.1-2","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.1-2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"73fbca9db73e65a64f40a36e950085ced93e56677d8d21f237c3b0558e4a3d4f","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.1-2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5998,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.1-2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.1-2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.3","r":"Ps.5.3","rawR":"Ps.5.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.3","value":"Ps.5.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist begins and ends each day with prayer, awaiting new expressions of God’s fidelity and goodness (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.143.8","r":"Ps.143.8","rawR":"Ps.143.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.143.8","value":"Ps.143.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"143:8"},"). • ",{"c":["wait expectantly:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The psalmist does not demand God’s grace but places hope in it (see ",{"href":"?bref=Mic.7.7","r":"Mic.7.7","rawR":"Mic.7.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.7.7","value":"Mic.7.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mic 7:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Hab.2.1","r":"Hab.2.1","rawR":"Hab.2.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hab.2.1","value":"Hab.2.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hab 2:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0a6292e44f761dcb003c814e53c13ad81dab7a01cce0eab855c6f73c566b1445","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5999,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.5","r":"Ps.5.5","rawR":"Ps.5.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.5","value":"Ps.5.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["the proud:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Mockers (see ",{"href":"?item=Ps.1.1_StudyNote_Filament","id":"Ps.1.1_StudyNote_Filament","rawId":"Ps.1.1_StudyNote_Filament","t":"link","v":"study note on 1:1"},"), the wicked (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.73.3","r":"Ps.73.3","rawR":"Ps.73.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.73.3","value":"Ps.73.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"73:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.75.4","r":"Ps.75.4","rawR":"Ps.75.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.75.4","value":"Ps.75.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"75:4"},"), and the arrogant (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.10.2","r":"Ps.10.2","rawR":"Ps.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.10.2","value":"Ps.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:2"},") use their mouths to twist truth and challenge the faith of the godly. • The Lord allows only the godly into his ",{"c":["presence"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.1.5","r":"Ps.1.5","rawR":"Ps.1.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.1.5","value":"Ps.1.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:5"},"). His holiness and justice do not tolerate oppression or those ",{"c":["who do evil"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},". • ",{"c":["you hate:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The Lord rejects proud sinners (see also ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.11.5","r":"Ps.11.5","rawR":"Ps.11.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.11.5","value":"Ps.11.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.5","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0a4f7cb1fe980acc77a962787eace0200bc1089addf9258d858974218aea5c18","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6000,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.5","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.7","r":"Ps.5.7","rawR":"Ps.5.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.7","value":"Ps.5.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," God promises his ",{"c":["unfailing love"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},"—his covenant goodness and faithfulness—to his people (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.25.6","r":"Ps.25.6","rawR":"Ps.25.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.25.6","value":"Ps.25.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.69.16","r":"Ps.69.16","rawR":"Ps.69.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.69.16","value":"Ps.69.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"69:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lam.3.32","r":"Lam.3.32","rawR":"Lam.3.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lam.3.32","value":"Lam.3.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lam 3:32"},"). • ",{"c":["your house:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The godly long to come into God’s presence with reverence and awe (see ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.12.28","r":"Heb.12.28","rawR":"Heb.12.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.12.28","value":"Heb.12.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 12:28"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.7","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"837ce34f9cfa445cbadb9b382fe834d2de76aeedd40d0a631614d7610569c3a6","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6001,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.8","r":"Ps.5.8","rawR":"Ps.5.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.8","value":"Ps.5.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:8"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," God guides those who are obedient, submissive, and patient in waiting for him to ",{"c":["lead"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," provide, and protect them (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.11","r":"Ps.27.11","rawR":"Ps.27.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.11","value":"Ps.27.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.3","r":"Ps.43.3","rawR":"Ps.43.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.3","value":"Ps.43.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.143.10","r":"Ps.143.10","rawR":"Ps.143.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.143.10","value":"Ps.143.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"143:10"},"), not those who expect God simply to endorse their own decisions. • Following ",{"c":["the right path"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," of wisdom leads to the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.11","r":"Ps.27.11","rawR":"Ps.27.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.11","value":"Ps.27.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.61.2","r":"Ps.61.2","rawR":"Ps.61.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.61.2","value":"Ps.61.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"61:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.139.24","r":"Ps.139.24","rawR":"Ps.139.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.139.24","value":"Ps.139.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"139:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.8","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":8,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":8}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.8","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e4496310fe496e44b89940d125f6848b0d3ce18da9bb6c6348a0b42dd659bdd1","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.8","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6002,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.8","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.8","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.9-10","r":"Ps.5.9-10","rawR":"Ps.5.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.9-10","value":"Ps.5.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:9-10"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist again describes the vile acts of the wicked, who cannot stand in God’s presence."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.9-10","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":10,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":9}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.9-10","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ecda467b4ffc2e35e57cd6f50bd7d772360d86b8945dadddefab3fabb3e725e0","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.9-10","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6003,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.9-10","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.9-10","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.10","r":"Ps.5.10","rawR":"Ps.5.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.10","value":"Ps.5.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:10"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist prays for the justice and retribution that God promised against the wicked (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.1.6","r":"Ps.1.6","rawR":"Ps.1.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.1.6","value":"Ps.1.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:6"},")—those who have ",{"c":["rebelled against"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," the Lord. • The wicked lay ",{"c":["traps"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," to kill (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.38.12","r":"Ps.38.12","rawR":"Ps.38.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.38.12","value":"Ps.38.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"38:12"},") or deceive (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.140.4-5","r":"Ps.140.4-5","rawR":"Ps.140.4-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.140.4-5","value":"Ps.140.4-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"140:4-5"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.10","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":10,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":10}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.10","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"07cc763df299b7f1b3f62ae68bb87d7ff0e1920b7a3777cf0432075c2d4b2348","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.10","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6004,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.10","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.10","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.11","r":"Ps.5.11","rawR":"Ps.5.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.11","value":"Ps.5.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:11"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," A blessing rests on ",{"c":["all who take refuge in"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," God (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.18.30","r":"Ps.18.30","rawR":"Ps.18.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.18.30","value":"Ps.18.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:30"},"). • Joy and praise make good companions. The godly ",{"c":["rejoice"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," when they see evidence of God’s rescue. They ",{"c":["sing joyful praises"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," as a new song (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.33.3","r":"Ps.33.3","rawR":"Ps.33.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.33.3","value":"Ps.33.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"33:3"},"). When the Lord restores peace to this world, puts down evil, and rewards the righteous, they will have lasting ",{"c":["joy"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.9.2-4","r":"Ps.9.2-4","rawR":"Ps.9.2-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.9.2-4","value":"Ps.9.2-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:2-4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.53.6","r":"Ps.53.6","rawR":"Ps.53.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.53.6","value":"Ps.53.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"53:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.90.14-15","r":"Ps.90.14-15","rawR":"Ps.90.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.90.14-15","value":"Ps.90.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"90:14-15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.118.24","r":"Ps.118.24","rawR":"Ps.118.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.118.24","value":"Ps.118.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"118:24"},"). • The children of God, who find refuge in him, ",{"c":["love"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," his ",{"c":["name"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},". To love his name is to love his very character."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.11","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":11,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":11}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.11","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"04c54ff2b494d2496868ad2b19e83ee4bd92d48cf0ecebbfcf417d01ff909ffd","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.11","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6005,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.11","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.11","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.12","r":"Ps.5.12","rawR":"Ps.5.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.12","value":"Ps.5.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:12"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist extends his concern beyond himself to all the ",{"c":["godly."],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," • A ",{"c":["shield"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," here an image of God’s protection, deflects spears and arrows from its bearer."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.5.12","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":5,"endVerse":12,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":12}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.5.12","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"349077dc2af4a2305bed8ec8cc69e63b2cdc056872da861a27452fa8412b2549","sourceItemName":"Ps.5.12","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6006,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.5.12","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.5.12","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}